LowCode is an autonomous coding agent for Android, built on the same LowFrame account and action protocol
as the LowCode VS Code extension. Sign in, pick a project folder on your device, and chat with it about
what you want built — it writes real files into that folder for you, asking before every write and asking
you clarifying questions when something is genuinely ambiguous. There's no shell on stock Android, so it
can't run build commands like the desktop version — it focuses purely on writing the files your project
needs.
